title: A Letter from Bamberg
subtitle: Some of Hoffmann's ministers send feelers.
view-if: crisis_bavaria = 1 and bav_talks_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; bav_talks_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= A Letter from Bamberg

A Social Democratic railwayman has crossed the lines with a letter. Some of Hoffmann's ministers do not want Prussian troops to conquer a Bavarian city. They hint at terms: the councils dissolved, an amnesty for the rank and file, the leaders before a court.

- @talk: Open talks through Toller.
- @towns: Print the letter for the Social Democratic workers of the towns.
- @refuse: Refuse to talk to the government of the Freikorps.

@talk
subtitle: It may save lives later. The Whites will learn that Munich is weakening.
on-arrival: bav_talks += 1; lean_unionist += 2

Toller meets Hoffmann's envoys in a village inn. Nothing is signed.

@towns
subtitle: Social Democratic workers in the towns will learn that their own ministers are bargaining. Some will come over.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_army += 3;
Q.bav_peasants += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000 men';
!}

In Rosenheim and Kolbermoor the workers' councils declare for Munich and send armed men.

@refuse
subtitle: The workers of Munich do not bargain over their own surrender.
on-arrival: militancy += 3; lean_offensive += 1
